Read-only verification of the installed Bonus Drain scheduler. Do not modify code,
configuration, cache, queue state, units, or timers. Do not refresh provider usage.

1. Resolve `${BONUS_DRAIN_BIN:-$HOME/.local/bin/bonus-drain}` and run `doctor --json`,
   `status --json`, `gates --json`, and `plan --json`. All must select the same validated
   config and XDG database. Stop and report if lifecycle ownership, config, or an ambiguous
   claim requires reconciliation.
2. From cached account snapshots, report freshness, exact reset, gate reason, and planned
   concrete provider/account independently. Missing or stale data is closed/unknown, never
   zero usage. Do not invoke any configured usage adapter.
3. Inspect the current-cycle queue/runs JSON. Confirm no task has more than one accounted
   launch for an eligibility key, every new launch persists a concrete non-`auto` provider
   and account, and dispatched work has either a terminal event or an explicit live router
   job. An ambiguous claim is neither success nor a known failure.
4. Read `systemctl --user status` and the last ten hours of journal for
   `bonus-drain-refresh.service` and `bonus-drain-scout.service`. Confirm the timer identities
   are self-owned, refresh precedes scout, and the observed scout decision matches the cached
   plan. No dispatch is a valid result when every gate is closed.
5. Confirm the Bonus-only and combined viewers use the stable CLI/XDG database and normalized
   cache only. A page request must not run a provider, usage, activation, or refresh command.

Print a concise evidence summary with each provider/account reported separately, any orphan
or duplicate called out explicitly, and unknown data described as unverified. Then stop.
